  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Aligned with TestFramework.Core 0.4.0's run contract, plus a hardening pass: artifact file IO now honours the run's deadline token, so a stalled read or write stops when the step does. Rooted-but-not-fully-qualified paths (\"\\results\\out.txt\", \"C:out.txt\") are refused by name instead of silently escaping the run directory onto the current drive. The run-directory cleanup only ever removes a directory RunDirectoryStep itself created, a second UseRunDirectory() in one run is refused, and FindArtifact refuses a folder holding more than one file instead of taking the first by enumeration order - use FindArtifacts for a folder of many. Declared IO contracts now state variable inputs as required, so a missing producer is refused at plan time with the fix named. Requires TestFramework.Core 0.4.0.",
